,"api_error_status":null,"result":"An ETF's expense ratio is **never billed to you directly**. It is deducted from the fund's assets.\n\n**How it works:**\n- **Daily accrual:** The annual rate is divided across the year. A 0.10% ratio accrues about 0.10%/365 of fund assets each day.\n- **Paid from fund assets:** The fund pays the sponsor, custodian, administrator and other providers out of its holdings, usually monthly. Dividend income received by the fund often covers it first.\n- **Reflected in NAV:** Because the accrued fees are a liability on the fund's books, they slightly lower the net asset value per share. Your share price and returns are therefore reported *net* of fees.\n\n**What this means for you:**\n- No line item appears on your brokerage statement.\n- The cost shows up as a small, steady drag on performance relative to the underlying index.\n- You pay only for the days you hold the shares.\n\nTrading costs such as commissions and bid-ask spreads are separate and are not part of the expense ratio.","ttft_ms":1520,"type":"result","duration_ms":4938,"uuid":"84cf4803-20a1-492f-9de4-25a077cc1be6","ttft_stream_ms":1463,"time_to_request_ms":51,"first_content_frame_ms":1463,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
